  "label": "Propaganda",
  "description": "The meme functions as a form of propaganda, which is a technique used to influence public opinion or behavior through selective presentation of information. This concept is rooted in historical and political contexts, such as wartime messaging, political campaigns, and social media activism. The visual of distress combined with the text is a common propaganda tactic to evoke emotional responses and reinforce a moral stance.",
